# The API the browser calls. `api.` — the proxied host — NOT the raw Railway one.
#
# It was `kartavaya-production.up.railway.app` from 2026-08-29, and that was
# right at the time: `api.kartavaya.com` still resolved to Vercel anycast and
# returned 404, so nothing could depend on it. That was fixed on 2026-09-04 and
# the fallback was never revisited.
#
# ⚠ A raw `*.up.railway.app` host is a bad thing to put in a shipped bundle.
# It is outside Cloudflare, it is a well-known target for ISP and corporate DNS
# blocking, and when it IS blocked the browser gets no HTTP response at all —
# which `Protected.jsx` can only render as "Could not reach Kartavaya", the one
# failure the product cannot explain to the user or log.
#
# Re-measured before this switch, 2026-09-08: `api.kartavaya.com` answers
# `/api/health` with real API JSON, its `/api/auth/me` preflight returns the
# correct `access-control-allow-origin` + credentials for `https://app.
# kartavaya.com`, a bad token gets a clean 401 rather than a network error, and
# both container origins (`https://localhost`, `capacitor://localhost`) are
# admitted. `public/_headers` already allows BOTH hosts in `connect-src`, so no
# CSP change is needed and a rollback here needs no second edit.
#
# The rate-limiting objection is spent: proxying `api.` once gave every visitor
# behind one Cloudflare edge a shared bucket, and that was fixed and measured
# working on 2026-08-31 (401 x5 then 429, keyed per caller).
#
# ⚠ THIS FILE MAY NOT BE WHAT PRODUCTION USES. Cloudflare Pages injects
# `VITE_BACKEND_URL` as a real env var, and Vite gives an injected var
# precedence over every `.env` file — so no commit can override it and only the
# Pages dashboard can. If the dashboard still holds the Railway URL, this line
# changes nothing. Verify in the DEPLOYED chunk, never in this file.
VITE_BACKEND_URL=https://api.kartavaya.com

# Where the landing page's "Request a demo" button goes.
#
# Without this, `pages/marketing/cta.js` hides the button and shows the
# invite-only note instead — deliberately, because the product has no public
# signup and pointing the CTA at /login strands visitors on a password field
# for an account they do not have.
#
# TEST NUMBER, not the business line. +44 7405 382925 is the owner's own
# number, set so the WhatsApp path can be exercised end to end before a
# business account exists. `wa.me` takes the number with no +, spaces or
# dashes.
#
# SWAP THIS before the landing page is advertised anywhere. A public CTA
# pointing at a personal UK mobile is fine for a staging walkthrough and wrong
# for Indian accounting firms arriving from a marketing link. The previous
# value, `mailto:hello@aekaminc.com`, is the safe fallback if the business
# number is not ready in time.
VITE_LEAD_CTA_HREF=https://wa.me/447405382925

# The invoice host. `payLink()` in `pages/ganit/_shared.jsx` falls back to
# `window.location.origin` when this is unset — which, for staff working inside
# the product, meant every copied invoice link read `app.kartavaya.com/i/<token>`
# and was sent to a customer on the app's origin. That is the one thing
# `pay.` exists to prevent: `email_service.py:25` keeps the invoice on its own
# host so it "can never be mistaken for a session".
#
# Emailed invoices were never wrong — those come from the backend's PAY_URL
# (`services/invoice_email.py:53`). This fixes the in-app copy/share button.
#
# Deliberately NOT set in .env.development: on localhost the fallback is
# correct, because this origin is the only host that can serve the link.
VITE_PAY_BASE_URL=https://pay.kartavaya.com
